 {"name": "AlgebraicGeometry.ThetaGeneratorSeed.seedUnivRDN_of_forall_germ_mem_span", "kind": "theorem", "signature": "theorem seedUnivRDN_of_forall_germ_mem_span (hgerm : \u2200 (z : relCurve C (seedChartRing C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j)), \u2200 \u2983\u03c8 : relThetaSections C (seedChartRing C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j) \u03c0 (windowM_choice \u03c0 h\u03c0 g)\u2984, \u03c8 \u2208 divUniversalSeedK C \u03c0 h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j \u2192 ((relCurve C (seedChartRing C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j)).presheaf.germ (relPinnedChart C (seedChartRing C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j) \u03c0 ((seedUniv C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j hO h\u03c7).side z)) z (seedUniv_mem_chart C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j hO h\u03c7 z)).hom (relThetaResSide (windowM_choice \u03c0 h\u03c0 g) ((seedUniv C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j hO h\u03c7).side z) (le_rfl) \u03c8) \u2208 Ideal.span {((relCurve C (seedChartRing C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j)).presheaf.germ (relPinnedChart C (seedChartRing C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j) \u03c0 ((seedUniv C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j hO h\u03c7).side z)) z (seedUniv_mem_chart C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j hO h\u03c7 z)).hom (relThetaResSide (windowM_choice \u03c0 h\u03c0 g) ((seedUniv C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j hO h\u03c7).side z) (le_rfl) ((seedUniv C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j hO h\u03c7).sec z))}) : SeedUnivRDN C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j hO h\u03c7", "doc": "**`SeedUnivRDN` from seed-level germ divisibility** (I-0305 \u00a7route, the assembly): the universal seed's RD-N holds provided that, at every point `z`, every window reading `read \u03c8` (`\u03c8 \u2208 K_univ`) has its germ at `z` in the principal ideal generated by the germ of the achiever section's reading `read (sec z)` in the stalk `\ud835\udcaa_z`.  This is the achiever's single-point local generation at `z` (`read sec z` attains the base multiplicity, I-0291) transported to the total-space germ.  The proof instantiates the per-point germ reduction `notMem_support_chartColengthModule_of_forall_germ_mem_span` at the seed's colength (`K := divUniversalSeedK`, finite over `R_Z` by `finite_divUniversalSeedK`), whose support-avoidance is exactly `SeedUnivRDN z`.  Single-point throughout, so the degree obstruction (I-0305 \u00a72) never fires; the sole remaining wall is the germ-divisibility premise (the fibre-DVR \u2192 germ base change).", "library": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild", "file": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/DivSchemeRedesignKappaZSeed.lean", "line": 96}
 {"name": "AlgebraicGeometry.ThetaGeneratorSeed.seedUnivRDN_of_forall_kappaZ_tensor_subsingleton", "kind": "theorem", "signature": "theorem seedUnivRDN_of_forall_kappaZ_tensor_subsingleton (hfib : \u2200 (z : relCurve C (seedChartRing C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j)), Subsingleton (\u21a5(chartColengthModule (divUniversalSeedK C \u03c0 h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j) ((seedUniv C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j hO h\u03c7).side z) ((seedUniv C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j hO h\u03c7).sec z)) \u2297[ \u0393(relCurve C (seedChartRing C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j), relPinnedChart C (seedChartRing C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j) \u03c0 ((seedUniv C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j hO h\u03c7).side z))] ((isAffineOpen_relPinnedChart C (seedChartRing C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j) \u03c0 ((seedUniv C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j hO h\u03c7).side z)).primeIdealOf \u27e8z, seedUniv_mem_chart C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j hO h\u03c7 z\u27e9).asIdeal.ResidueField)) : SeedUnivRDN C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j hO h\u03c7", "doc": "**`SeedUnivRDN` from the sharp point fibre.**  The support criterion can also be fed directly by the single-point tensor `chartColengthModule K_univ ... \u2297_{\u0393(V)} \u03ba(z)`.  This is deliberately independent of the fibre-to-total germ transport: it records the exact module-theoretic insertion point for a future residue-field proof, with `\u03ba(z)` taken from the chart point prime itself (never from the comapped base prime).", "library": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild", "file": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/DivSchemeRedesignKappaZSeed.lean", "line": 133}
